#
# Bug#39905175 Bound query expansion during parsing
#
# Every reference to a CTE after the first one reparses the CTE
# definition. With chains of CTEs that each reference the previous
# one twice, the number of reparses grows exponentially with the
# chain depth. Building a statement is limited to 1024 CTE reparses
# and view parses, and 64 MiB of cumulative definition text.
#
# A chain c0..cN where each ck references c(k-1) twice, referenced
# twice by the outer query, needs 2^(N+2) - N - 3 reparses.
# N=8 needs 1013 reparses; each extra reference to c0 adds one.
# 1013 reparses: accepted
a
1
# 1024 reparses: accepted
a
1
# 1025 reparses: rejected
ERROR HY000: Query expansion exceeded an implementation limit. Simplify the query.
# Deep nesting (about 2^32 reparses) is rejected quickly
ERROR HY000: Query expansion exceeded an implementation limit. Simplify the query.
# The same connection recovers after a rejection
a
1
# Byte limit: a CTE with about 1 MiB of text may be reparsed 63 times
# (64 references), but not 64 times (65 references).
